erator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": " Fifteen student and youth organizations. Thirty-five other organizations. That breakdown is the starting point for understanding the network behind the unrest in France examined by Fox News Digital\u2019s Asra Nomani. Of the 50 organizations she identified, just 30 percent were student or youth groups. The remaining 70 percent included labor unions, political parties, and other adult organizations, many she identified as communist, socialist, or far left.  Calling this simply a student uprising leaves the public with an incomplete picture of who was involved. Young people\u2019s concerns may provide the movement\u2019s public face, while established political organizations bring their own agendas, infrastructure, and ambitions. The accountability question is straightforward: Who is speaking for students, and who is using students to advance a separate political project? ", "large_image": "BcqvUznTDrY2FSHn.png", "title": "The Far Left Network Behind France\u2019s Student Protest Narrative"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2111672976093716627", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVjbtKi8", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 79, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8893048, "raw_content": "", "author": "rdvs34283", "created": 1792363761812, "profile_picture": "p9HQtdiLq2uP", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Tikk", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVjbtKi8.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/craigkellyafee/status/2111672976093716627", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Paris\u2019 Galeries Lafayette is the most beautif